{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310667,"nonce":"hCPo5k7v6Xnz2A/XMtQX+tvBcy8=","title":"case A(id)|B(id): or-patterns silently dropped every alternative after the first — FIXED in 3227708","message":"`case A(id) | B(id):` worked only for `A` — `B` and beyond fell through (exhaustiveness warned \"missing variants: B\" and runtime sometimes SIGILL'd, depending on enum layout).\n\nThree independent gaps, fixed in `3227708`:\n\n1. **Parser** ([parser/src/rd/expr.rs:1120](parser/src/rd/expr.rs#L1120)) — `parse_case_pattern` parsed exactly one pattern atom and never consulted `|`. `Pattern::Or` existed in the AST enum but was never constructed. Wrapped the existing logic into `parse_case_pattern_atom` and added a `parse_case_pattern` that loops on `TokenKind::Pipe`.\n\n2. **TAST `create_constructor_expression_with_bindings`** ([compiler/src/tast/ast_lowering.rs:13651](compiler/src/tast/ast_lowering.rs#L13651)) — no `Pattern::Or` arm; the `_` fallback called `lower_pattern_to_expression` which only returned the first alternative. Added an `Or` arm that creates a `PatternPlaceholder` preserving the full Or pattern.\n\n3. **TAST→HIR `lower_parser_pattern_to_hir_with_bindings`** ([compiler/src/ir/tast_to_hir.rs:4143](compiler/src/ir/tast_to_hir.rs#L4143)) — no `Pattern::Or` arm; `_ =\u003e HirPattern::Wildcard` collapsed Or to wildcard. Also `has_constructor_patterns` checked only `Pattern::Constructor`, missing `Or(Constructor, ...)` — routed the switch through the value-equality if-else chain instead of the constructor-pattern path. Added recursive `pattern_contains_constructor` helper.\n\n**MIR layer was already correct** — `lower_pattern_test` for `HirPattern::Or` ORs the alternatives' discriminant checks, and `collect_variants_from_pattern` recurses for exhaustiveness. The Or pattern just had to reach MIR intact.\n\n**Binding limitation:** `bind_pattern` for `Or` uses only the first alternative's extraction. Works for the common case where all alternatives have the same field shape at the same positions (e.g. `U8(id) | I8(id) | U32(id) | I64(id)`) — boxed enums share `[tag:i32][pad:i32][field0:i64]...` layout, so field 0's offset/width is identical across variants. Or-patterns whose alternatives have *different* field shapes (rare) need a phi over the discriminant test — separate follow-up.\n\n**How to apply:** if a user reports that `case A | B:` only matches `A`, or sees \"missing variants: B\" on a pattern that visibly covers B, this is the path. Test by stripping to a 2-variant or-pattern and inspecting whether HirPattern::Or makes it to MIR.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_or_pattern_dropped` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}